<title>UK: Unionists say no change to UK voting policy.</title>
<headline>Unionists say no change to UK voting policy.</headline>
<dateline>BELFAST 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Ireland's chief Protestant party said on Monday it would support Sir James Goldsmith's Europe of the Nations Group in the European parliament but said the move would not affect its voting policy in the British parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;We will continue to vote in the same way we do and have done in the House (of Commons)...we will be voting as Ulster Unionists,&quot; David Trimble, leader of the Ulster Unionist Party told a news conference.</p>
</text>
